1
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:11,546
-==www.RagBear.com==-
是, 首相  第1季第8集

2
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,747
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=-
翻译: vivitata
校对: tpring
时间轴: T-boy

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
我们的人

5
00:00:43,313 --> 00:00:45,100
你好啊 亲爱的
Hello, darling!

6
00:00:45,873 --> 00:00:48,467
啊 是新闻 讲到我了吗?
Ah, the news! Got to me yet?

7
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:50,376
没有 你又干什么了?
No. What have you done now?

8
00:00:50,377 --> 00:00:52,322
好激烈的质询 他们攻击
A sensational Question Time. People were attacking

9
00:00:52,357 --> 00:00:54,399
我控制军费的计划
me about my controlling defence expenditure

10
00:00:54,434 --> 00:00:55,783
被我驳了个落花流水
I really made mincemeat of them.

11
00:00:55,784 --> 00:00:57,207
新闻还没提呢
They haven't mentioned it yet.

12
00:00:57,953 --> 00:01:00,173
典型BBC作风      这不是BBC
Typical BBC.        It's not BBC.

13
00:01:00,513 --> 00:01:02,420
典型ITV(独立台)作风      这是4频道
Typical ITV.       It's Channel 4.

14
00:01:02,715 --> 00:01:04,036
那还能指望什么?
Well, what can you expect?

15
00:01:04,037 --> 00:01:07,135
快完了      开大点声
It has only several minutes to go.        Turn it up, then.

16
00:01:08,022 --> 00:01:10,669
对本琪命运的担忧日益增长
There's growing anxiety for the fate of Benji,

17
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:12,301
这条老英国牧羊犬
an 0ld English sheepdog,

18
00:01:12,401 --> 00:01:14,227
昨夜穿过铁丝网
who last night got under the wire

19
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:18,302
闯入索尔兹伯里平原炮兵靶场
and into the artillery range on Salisbury Plain.

20
00:01:18,673 --> 00:01:21,601
本琪的主人是8岁女童琳达弗莱彻
Benji belongs to 8-year-old Linda Fletcher.

21
00:01:21,701 --> 00:01:24,491
琳达去年在车祸中失去了双亲
Linda lost both her parents in a car crash.

22
00:01:24,526 --> 00:01:26,629
只有本吉和她活了下来
Both she and Benji survived.

23
00:01:27,273 --> 00:01:29,859
不幸的是 该区域遍布着未爆弹
Unfortunately, the area is full of unexploded shells

24
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:33,608
险象环生 只有一条安全道路
and is highly dangerous except for one fixed road.

25
00:01:33,643 --> 00:01:37,023
本琪距该路甚远 似已迷路
Benji is a long way from the road and seems to be lost.

26
00:01:37,193 --> 00:01:38,620
军方深表遗憾
The Army expressed their regrets,

27
00:01:38,621 --> 00:01:40,792
但同时表示 除非它回到道路上
but say that unless he comes to the road

28
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,144
否则他们无能为力
otherwise there's nothing they can do.

29
00:01:43,773 --> 00:01:47,768
若无意外 它将很快饿死或被炸死
If nothing happens soon he will either starve or be blown up

30
00:01:48,513 --> 00:01:49,917
琳达决心
Linda is preparing to

31
00:01:49,918 --> 00:01:52,117
在靶场外再守一夜
spend another night's vigil on Salisbury Plain,

32
00:01:52,217 --> 00:01:54,446
盼望本琪归来
hoping that Benji will come back.

33
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,380
晚间新闻播送完了
And that's the news this evening.

34
00:01:59,153 --> 00:02:02,145
你肯定从头看到尾了吗?      肯定
Are you sure you watched all of the news?        Yes.

35
00:02:02,313 --> 00:02:03,804
真的一点都没提我?
Was it on, the bit about me?

36
00:02:03,805 --> 00:02:05,407
没有 除非我看漏了
No. Unless I missed it of course

37
00:02:05,442 --> 00:02:06,545
你说你看全了的
You said you watched it all.

38
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:11,339
可你知道 人总会自动无视无聊的部分嘛
But one mentally tunes out the boring bits.

39
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:14,640
不是说你 亲爱的 你不无聊
Not you, dear. You're not boring.

40
00:02:14,641 --> 00:02:17,629
至少对我不会 就算全国人民都这么想
Not to me,even if you are to the rest of the country.

41
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:19,856
亲爱的 英国国防大计正在
The future defence of Britain was being

42
00:02:19,857 --> 00:02:22,415
全民论坛上引发激辩
fought out in the great forum of the nation

43
00:02:22,993 --> 00:02:24,126
结果观众看到什么?
and what do they give the viewers?

44
00:02:24,127 --> 00:02:26,040
真人版"灵犬莱希"
A rerun of ''Lassie Come Home''!

45
00:02:27,433 --> 00:02:30,425
我觉得军方应该出面救狗
I think the Army ought to rescue that dog.

46
00:02:30,633 --> 00:02:32,244
每天都有孩子丢狗
Kids lose dogs every day.

47
00:02:32,245 --> 00:02:35,086
军队救得过来吗?
Should the Army rescue every one of them?

48
00:02:35,121 --> 00:02:37,154
你不懂平头百姓的心
You don't understand ordinary people feel.

49
00:02:37,254 --> 00:02:39,369
我正是一名平头百姓
I happen to be an ordinary person myself.

50
00:02:39,469 --> 00:02:43,868
不会吧      你要我浪费纳税人的钱
Oh, surely not        You want me to waste taxpayers' money

51
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:46,388
收买便宜人心?
on buying a bit of cheap popularity?

52
00:02:46,553 --> 00:02:47,305
有时候你非得做些经济上不合算的事
Sometimes you have to do things

53
00:02:47,306 --> 00:02:50,750
这就是文明社会
that aren't economic in a civilised society.

54
00:02:51,273 --> 00:02:53,210
写成报告提交财政部啊
Write a paper on that and submit it to the Treasury.

55
00:02:53,211 --> 00:02:54,213
内阁经济委员会
We don't get many laughs

56
00:02:54,214 --> 00:02:55,779
正愁没笑话听呢
in the cabinet of economic communitee

57
00:02:58,313 --> 00:03:00,168
军情五处处长来了 首相
The Director General of MI5, Prime Minister.

58
00:03:00,169 --> 00:03:02,872
你好 杰弗里 快进来
Ah, hello, Geoffrey. Come along in.

59
00:03:03,273 --> 00:03:05,304
谢谢 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

60
00:03:05,833 --> 00:03:08,470
请问能不能...
Eh, I wonder if...

61
00:03:08,570 --> 00:03:12,543
没关系 我的会晤伯纳都在场 对吧伯纳?
Oh, that's all right. I always have Bernard present.

62
00:03:12,753 --> 00:03:14,190
这次不行 首相
Not this time, Prime Minister.

63
00:03:14,191 --> 00:03:18,567
啊 我也不一定要伯纳在场的 对吧
Ah. I don't always have Bernard present.

64
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:24,906
请坐 我没收到这次会晤的文件
Do sit down. I don't have any papers for this meeting.

65
00:03:25,073 --> 00:03:28,111
是没有 太严重了      怎么?
No, it's too serious.        Why?

66
00:03:29,273 --> 00:03:31,161
我们刚收到一些情报
We've just received some information.

67
00:03:31,162 --> 00:03:32,552
你们不就干这个的吗?
Isn't that what you're supposed to do?

68
00:03:34,233 --> 00:03:35,400
您知道约翰霍斯特吗?
Do you know John Halsted?

69
00:03:35,401 --> 00:03:39,376
你前任 60年代军情五处首脑 上个月死了
Your predecessor.The header of MI5 in '60s. Died last month.

70
00:03:39,713 --> 00:03:41,987
他把全部私人文件留给了我们
He left his personal papers to us.

71
00:03:41,988 --> 00:03:43,351
我们刚开始审查
We've started to go through them.

72
00:03:43,369 --> 00:03:46,928
显然他五六十年代传过政府情报给莫斯科
It`s very clear he was passing government secrets to Moscow

73
00:03:46,929 --> 00:03:49,566
传了好几年
several years in the '50s and '60s.

74
00:03:49,638 --> 00:03:53,210
军情五处首脑? 是俄国间谍?
The head of MI5? A Russian agent?

75
00:03:53,211 --> 00:03:54,396
似乎是这样
So it seems.

76
00:03:55,273 --> 00:03:56,743
他干嘛留文件给你们?
Why did he leave his papers to you?

77
00:03:56,744 --> 00:03:59,708
遗嘱上说是临终良心发现
His will said it was a final act of conscience.

78
00:03:59,808 --> 00:04:02,425
我觉得是想死后出风头
I think it's just posthumous gloating.

79
00:04:03,109 --> 00:04:04,882
炫耀他没被抓住
Showing us he could get away with it.

80
00:04:04,968 --> 00:04:08,230
他泄露出去多少?      这倒无所谓
How much did he tell them?        That hardly matters.

81
00:04:08,265 --> 00:04:11,398
有了剑桥五人组和
I mean, with Burgess, McLean, Philby, Blake

82
00:04:11,399 --> 00:04:13,299
克罗格夫妇(波特兰间谍网 1961)
and Fuchs and the Krogers,

83
00:04:13,913 --> 00:04:16,786
再多一个也没什么不同
one more didn't make much more difference.

84
00:04:17,513 --> 00:04:20,432
重点在于 他是我们的人      我们的人?
The point is he was one of us.        One of us?

85
00:04:20,532 --> 00:04:22,663
剑桥毕业直接入军情五处
Joined MI5 straight from Cambridge,

86
00:04:22,664 --> 00:04:24,630
一辈子做公务员
Being in the Civil Service all his life.

87
00:04:24,730 --> 00:04:25,749
一旦传出去
If this ever gets out,

88
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:30,453
他任内招募的人永远洗不清了
all of us recruited in his time will be suspects for ever.

89
00:04:31,113 --> 00:04:34,288
对啊...你该不是间谍吧?
Yes. ..You're not a spy, are you?

90
00:04:35,673 --> 00:04:38,363
开玩笑的 你真不是吧? 算了
Only joking. You're not, are you? No...

91
00:04:40,193 --> 00:04:40,863
不仅如此
This is not all.

92
00:04:40,864 --> 00:04:43,403
我们对约翰爵士发起过
We held an internal security investigation

93
00:04:43,404 --> 00:04:45,117
内部安全调查 在70年代
into Sir John in the '70s.

94
00:04:45,217 --> 00:04:48,138
媒体闹得满城风雨 记得吗?      好像有
There was a lot of speculation. Remember?        Vaguely.

95
00:04:48,238 --> 00:04:50,927
完全不负责任 空穴来风
All totally irresponsible and ill-informed.

96
00:04:51,153 --> 00:04:53,666
媒体指控他是间谍的事?      对
When the press suggested he was a spy?        Yes.

97
00:04:53,766 --> 00:04:55,934
他确实是啊      对 可他们又不知道
Well, he was.        But they didn't know that!

98
00:04:56,034 --> 00:04:58,805
他们一点不了解情况
They were being totally ignorant.

99
00:04:58,806 --> 00:05:01,490
也不负责 歪打正着罢了
They are not responsible. They just happened to be accurate.

100
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:07,158
总之 那次调查把他完全洗清了
Anyway, the inquiry cleared him completely,

101
00:05:07,193 --> 00:05:10,603
可他们忽略了些很明显的疑问和检查
but they missed some rather obvious questions and checks.

102
00:05:10,638 --> 00:05:13,993
所以显然...人们有所怀疑
So obvious that...well... One wonders.

103
00:05:14,093 --> 00:05:15,564
对
Yes.

104
00:05:16,913 --> 00:05:18,223
人们怀疑什么?
What does one wonder?

105
00:05:18,877 --> 00:05:22,949
人们怀疑那些洗清他的家伙
One wonders about the chaps who cleared him.

106
00:05:23,113 --> 00:05:26,662
对啊 他们会不会太蠢 是吗?
I see. Whether they were stupid, you mean?

107
00:05:26,873 --> 00:05:30,183
不 首相 他们会不会也是...
No, Prime Minister. Whether they were also...

108
00:05:30,393 --> 00:05:33,385
间谍? 天啊
Spies?! My God!

109
00:05:33,553 --> 00:05:35,222
谁主持的调查?
Who headed that inquiry?

110
00:05:35,223 --> 00:05:38,180
老麦维爵士 可他当时身患重病
Old Lord MacIver, but he was ill a lot.

111
00:05:38,513 --> 00:05:40,811
好吧 其实是老糊涂了
Well, ga-ga, actually.

112
00:05:40,812 --> 00:05:44,285
所以实际上 是他秘书在主持
So, effectively, it was the secretary who conducted it.

113
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:48,567
秘书是谁?      汉弗莱阿普比
Who was the secretary?        Humphrey Appleby.

114
00:05:49,393 --> 00:05:52,450
汉弗莱?      正是 首相
Humphrey?        Yes, Prime Minister.

115
00:05:52,485 --> 00:05:54,134
你觉得他可能也是间谍?
You think he may have been a spy, too?

116
00:05:54,169 --> 00:05:56,779
有这个可能性 不过微乎其微
It's a remote possibility, but very unlikely.

117
00:05:56,879 --> 00:05:59,901
他总归是我们的人      约翰霍斯顿也是
After all he's one of us.        So was John Halsted.

118
00:06:00,599 --> 00:06:04,760
这倒是 不过没有别的证据对汉弗莱不利
Well, yes, but there's no other evidence against Humphrey.

119
00:06:04,795 --> 00:06:07,263
他会不会掩护了某个我们的人...
Might he have been covering up for one of us...

120
00:06:07,264 --> 00:06:09,098
他们的人...你们的人?
one of them...one of you?

121
00:06:09,473 --> 00:06:14,069
大概是吧 可我毫不怀疑他的忠诚
I suppose so, but I have no doubts at all about his loyalty.

122
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:16,539
更有可能他仅仅是...
It's much more likely to be just...

123
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,475
严重失职
Hideous incompetence.

124
00:06:18,509 --> 00:06:20,914
我们还没审完文件
We haven't been through the rest of his papers.

125
00:06:20,915 --> 00:06:24,044
您可以先对汉弗莱爵士发起调查
You could hold an inquiry into Sir Humphrey.

126
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:28,508
我可以吗?     虽然在这个阶段我不推荐
Could I?        Well, I wouldn't recommend it at this stage.

127
00:06:28,543 --> 00:06:31,547
消息可能泄露 不能再掀起不负责的媒体疑云了
We don't want more irresponsible speculation.

128
00:06:31,547 --> 00:06:34,576
就算是正确的      尤其是正确的
Even if it's accurate.        Especially if it's accurate.

129
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,538
最可怕的莫过于正确
There's nothing worse than accurate,

130
00:06:37,539 --> 00:06:40,102
不负责 空穴来风的媒体疑云了
irresponsible, ill-informed press speculation.

131
00:06:41,232 --> 00:06:43,888
您可以给汉弗莱放园艺假
You could send Humphrey off on gardening leave

132
00:06:43,889 --> 00:06:46,602
等我们审完霍斯顿文件
while we examine the rest of the Halsted papers.

133
00:06:46,678 --> 00:06:47,539
园艺假?
Gardening leave?

134
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,132
当然 然后您可以跟他当面对质
Certainly. And you could confront him.

135
00:06:50,232 --> 00:06:52,394
潜在证据全在这了
The substantive evidence is all here.

136
00:06:52,395 --> 00:06:54,228
要是他没什么嫌疑
Look. If you don't really suspect him.

137
00:06:54,229 --> 00:06:55,869
我们不能当没这回事吗?
Shouldn't we just forget about it?

138
00:06:55,904 --> 00:06:57,516
很显然 这取决于您
Well, obviously, it's your decision,

139
00:06:57,551 --> 00:07:00,838
可如果您不管
but on the other hand if you did nothing and it emerged later

140
00:07:00,839 --> 00:07:03,723
今后爆出来汉弗莱爵士真是...
that Sir Humphrey...that he was...

141
00:07:04,793 --> 00:07:07,899
他们的人 那可就不太好看了
..one of them, well, it might not look too good.

142
00:07:07,953 --> 00:07:11,654
更不用说作为内阁秘书
Not to mention that as Cabinet Secretary

143
00:07:11,655 --> 00:07:14,023
他也协调我们所有安全事宜
he co-ordinates our security services.

144
00:07:14,123 --> 00:07:17,544
什么也瞒不过他      有道理
There are no secrets from him.        You're right.

145
00:07:17,753 --> 00:07:19,596
可我真不敢相信
But I find it hard enough to believe

146
00:07:19,597 --> 00:07:21,343
一个我们的人 是个他们的人
that one of us was one of them.

147
00:07:23,302 --> 00:07:25,169
可如果两个我们的人 都是个他们的人
But if two of us were one of them...

148
00:07:27,913 --> 00:07:29,353
两个他们的人
Two of them.

149
00:07:30,273 --> 00:07:32,662
我们所有人就可能是...
..all of us could be, um...

150
00:07:32,873 --> 00:07:34,417
他们所有人
All of them.

151
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,155
谢谢 杰弗里 我听够了
Thank you, Geoffrey. I've heard enough.

152
00:07:39,313 --> 00:07:42,828
岂有此理 我们支持率又降3个点
Awful! Another three points down in the polls.

153
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:44,788
政府没有 只是您个人的支持率
Not the government. Only your personal rating.

154
00:07:46,566 --> 00:07:48,089
我犯了什么错?
What have I done wrong?

155
00:07:48,393 --> 00:07:51,543
低支持率通常表示您做得对
Low popularity usually means doing things right.

156
00:07:51,544 --> 00:07:53,762
不是因为我没削减军费吧?
It's not my failure to get defence cuts?

157
00:07:54,153 --> 00:07:56,929
老实说 首相 我觉得军费算不上
To be honest, I don't think defence cuts are the

158
00:07:56,930 --> 00:07:59,991
今天全国坊间热门话题
principal topic of conversation in supermarkets.

159
00:08:00,078 --> 00:08:01,958
不是军费 那是什么?
What is it if is not my defence policy?

160
00:08:01,959 --> 00:08:03,551
依大众媒体来看
To judge from the popular press,

161
00:08:03,586 --> 00:08:06,097
恐怕是索尔兹伯里平原上走丢的狗
I am afraid it's the lost dog on Salisbury Plain.

162
00:08:07,473 --> 00:08:09,752
也许政府需要个丢狗政策
Perhaps the government needs a lost dog policy.

163
00:08:11,153 --> 00:08:12,379
还有事吗 首相?
Is there anything else, Prime Minister?

164
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:15,444
对 还有一件事
Yes, there is something else.

165
00:08:15,503 --> 00:08:19,507
安全的事 伯纳 你不介意吧?
A security matter. Bernard, would you mind?

166
00:08:19,508 --> 00:08:20,847
什么?
I'm sorry?

167
00:08:31,913 --> 00:08:35,139
你干什么 伯纳?      我以为...
What are you doing?        Well, I thought...

168
00:08:35,187 --> 00:08:37,388
没有人 就是...
There wasn't anyone...that he's

169
00:08:37,389 --> 00:08:39,144
我是希望你回避一下
I was just hoping you'd leave us alone.

170
00:08:39,755 --> 00:08:47,182
但我没有...哦 好吧
But I haven't...Oh. Yes.

171
00:08:51,913 --> 00:08:54,108
首相      对了 汉弗莱
Prime Minister.        Yes, Humphrey.

172
00:08:55,513 --> 00:08:57,091
有件事我得跟你谈谈
There's something I want to talk to you about.

173
00:08:57,092 --> 00:09:00,540
一件...重要机密
Something...very secret.

174
00:09:05,113 --> 00:09:07,504
如果我也回避会好说些吗?
Would it be easier if I wasn't here?

175
00:09:13,313 --> 00:09:16,334
几年前 有一桩安全调查
A few years ago, there was a security inquiry.

176
00:09:16,369 --> 00:09:19,631
你记得约翰霍斯顿爵士的名字吗?
Does the name Sir John Halsted ring a bell?

177
00:09:19,666 --> 00:09:21,044
当然记得 实际上
Yes, of course. In fact,

178
00:09:21,045 --> 00:09:24,187
调查正是我本人主持的
I had to conduct the inquiry myself, virtually.

179
00:09:24,222 --> 00:09:27,913
你没查到什么疑点吗?      当然没有
And you found nothing incriminating?        Of course not.

180
00:09:27,948 --> 00:09:30,978
首先 约翰霍斯顿是我们的人
In the first place John Halsted was one of us.

181
00:09:30,979 --> 00:09:32,426
是我多年老友了
We'd been friends for years.

182
00:09:32,461 --> 00:09:34,868
其次 整件事都是媒体炒作出来的
In the second place The whole story was got up by the press

183
00:09:34,903 --> 00:09:38,121
第三 内部安全调查的宗旨
and in the third place the whole object of internal security

184
00:09:38,122 --> 00:09:39,921
就在于查不出证据
inquiries is to find no evidence.

185
00:09:40,553 --> 00:09:42,734
就算领土安全受到威胁?
Even if the security of the realm is at risk?

186
00:09:42,769 --> 00:09:44,893
首相 如果您真觉得
Prime Minister If you really believe the security of

187
00:09:44,894 --> 00:09:47,165
有威胁 该找政治保安处
the realm is at risk, you call in the Special Branch.

188
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,506
政府安全调查只是
Government security inquiries are only

189
00:09:49,507 --> 00:09:51,772
消灭媒体谣言用的
used for killing press stories.

190
00:09:51,869 --> 00:09:55,108
使得首相能在下院里宣布
They enable the PM to stand up in the House and say,

191
00:09:55,208 --> 00:09:56,513
"经全面调查"
"We held a fully inquiry"

192
00:09:56,514 --> 00:09:59,545
"这些指控毫无证据"
"and there is no evidence to substantiate these charges."

193
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:01,760
如果真查到疑点呢?
What if you have found something suspicious?

194
00:10:01,761 --> 00:10:04,700
首相 其实政府中一切都可疑
Practically everything happened in government is suspicious.

195
00:10:05,593 --> 00:10:07,325
您支走伯纳 私下跟我谈
The fact that you asked Bernard to leave us alone

196
00:10:07,326 --> 00:10:10,584
这就堪称可疑
for a secret conversation might be construed as suspicious.

197
00:10:10,619 --> 00:10:14,463
没错      不过总之 那件事纯属无稽之谈
Indeed.        But the whole story was clearly a nonsense.

198
00:10:14,633 --> 00:10:17,352
典型舰队街(英国报界)的煽风点火
Typical Fleet Street sensationalism.

199
00:10:17,553 --> 00:10:21,328
那么约翰爵士不可能给俄国传了情报?
So he wasn't passing secrets to Moscow?

200
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,266
不可能 没有的事
Impossible. Out of the question.

201
00:10:23,266 --> 00:10:26,306
你敢以名誉担保?      毫无疑问
You'd stake your reputation on it?        Without hesitation

202
00:10:26,393 --> 00:10:29,854
这样啊 好吧 很遗憾告诉你
I see. Well, I'm afraid I have to tell you

203
00:10:29,855 --> 00:10:32,027
在他任内大半时间
that for a substantial part of his career

204
00:10:32,753 --> 00:10:34,472
他都是个俄国间谍
he was a Russian spy.

205
00:10:36,593 --> 00:10:39,491
我不相信 谁说的?
I don't believe it. Who says so?

206
00:10:39,504 --> 00:10:42,181
他自己 他留了所有文件给政府
He does. He left his papers to the government,

207
00:10:42,182 --> 00:10:45,458
包括一份详细自白书 军情五处已经证实了
including a detailed confession. MI5 agrees.

208
00:10:45,553 --> 00:10:47,124
从头至尾核对无误
It checks out all along the line.

209
00:10:48,313 --> 00:10:50,110
可是...
But...

210
00:10:50,273 --> 00:10:53,231
天啊 他...我说 他是...
Good Lord, he... I mean, he was...

211
00:10:53,433 --> 00:10:53,732
我们的人?
One of us?

212
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:57,724
正是 这会留下很多问题啊
Exactly This certainly leaves a lot of questions to be asked

213
00:10:57,824 --> 00:11:00,221
对 我先问你
Yes, and I'm asking you the first of them

214
00:11:00,222 --> 00:11:02,582
为什么没向他提很多问题?
why didn't you ask him a lot of questions?

215
00:11:04,793 --> 00:11:07,760
为什么调查那么快就洗清了他?
Why did the inquiry exonerate him so quickly?

216
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:12,933
我告诉您了 而且 我们当时很忙 再说...
I've already told you! Anyway, we were very busy. Besides...

217
00:11:14,513 --> 00:11:15,461
天啊 您不会觉得...
Good Lord! You don't think...?

218
00:11:15,462 --> 00:11:18,837
当然 不会有人怀疑...
I mean, surely nobody suspects...?

219
00:11:19,153 --> 00:11:20,935
我还能怎么办?
What else was I expected to do?

220
00:11:20,936 --> 00:11:23,347
你应该进行充分调查
You could have held a proper inquiry.

221
00:11:23,447 --> 00:11:24,629
你有证据证明
After all you had evidenced

222
00:11:24,630 --> 00:11:27,090
他有次停在南斯拉夫 时间长得出奇
a surprisingly long stay in Yugoslavia.

223
00:11:27,248 --> 00:11:28,248
所以呢?
Yes?

224
00:11:27,997 --> 00:11:31,431
不久 几个军情五处探员被捕了
Shortly afterwards, several MI5 agents behind the archon

225
00:11:31,432 --> 00:11:32,826
从此再没露面
were rounded up and never seen again.

226
00:11:33,012 --> 00:11:36,997
对...      他老是和一个翻译泡在一起
Yes...        He spent a lot of time with one interpreter.

227
00:11:37,032 --> 00:11:40,377
那翻译是个俄国间谍 对 我们知道
And she turned out to be a Russian agent.Yes.We knew that.

228
00:11:40,412 --> 00:11:43,059
大多数南斯拉夫翻译是俄国间谍
Most Yugoslav interpreters are Russian agents.

229
00:11:43,714 --> 00:11:46,174
如果不是中情局间谍的话
Those who aren't with the CIA, that is.

230
00:11:46,707 --> 00:11:47,695
你根本没追查
You never followed it up.

231
00:11:47,696 --> 00:11:50,082
我事情多得很
I had better things to do with my time.

232
00:11:50,193 --> 00:11:51,900
三个月后 她搬来英国
Three months later, she moved to England and

233
00:11:51,901 --> 00:11:53,709
在剑桥定居
settled in Cambridge,

234
00:11:54,345 --> 00:11:57,539
离约翰爵士家130米
150 yards from Sir John Halsted's house.

235
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,402
后来他们做了11年邻居
They were neighbours for the next 11 years.

236
00:12:00,953 --> 00:12:01,934
唉呀
Crikey!

237
00:12:04,313 --> 00:12:06,428
总不能什么都查吧
You can't check up on everything!

238
00:12:06,429 --> 00:12:08,822
没准会查出什么来呢
You never know what you might find!

239
00:12:09,273 --> 00:12:12,207
如果您真有所怀疑 就应该...
If you have such a suspicious mind. You ought to...

240
00:12:12,242 --> 00:12:13,656
发起安全调查
Hold security inquiries.

241
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:15,150
对...不
Ye...no!

242
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:20,410
约翰霍斯顿向我保证过 一位绅士的保证
John gave me his word. Halsted. The word of a gentleman.

243
00:12:20,445 --> 00:12:22,471
随便吧 汉弗莱 我有个问题了
Anyway, I have a problem.

244
00:12:22,472 --> 00:12:24,108
问题?      就是你
A problem?        You.

245
00:12:25,513 --> 00:12:28,107
我? 您该不会认为...
Me? You don't think...?

246
00:12:28,273 --> 00:12:30,662
您不可能认为...
You couldn't think...

247
00:12:31,673 --> 00:12:34,176
我一句俄语都不会说啊
I don't speak a word of Russian!

248
00:12:35,618 --> 00:12:38,737
可想而知 要么是失职 要么是串通
It must be either incompetence or collusion.

249
00:12:38,772 --> 00:12:41,504
串通? 我向您保证 首相 绝无串通
Collusion? I give you my word it wasn't collusion!

250
00:12:41,539 --> 00:12:46,423
绅士的保证?      没错 牛津的绅士
The word of a gentleman?        Exactly! An Oxford gentleman

251
00:12:48,170 --> 00:12:52,031
家里花园怎样?      哦 这个...
How's the garden?        Oh, well, it...

252
00:12:54,433 --> 00:12:56,713
首相 我求您 别给我园艺假
Prime Minister. I beseech you, not gardening leave.

253
00:12:56,714 --> 00:12:57,386
为什么?
Why not?

254
00:12:57,833 --> 00:12:59,830
我得保持名誉啊
I have my reputation to think of!

255
00:12:59,831 --> 00:13:02,512
你拿它担保霍斯顿的清白了
You've already staked that on Halsted's innocence.

256
00:13:02,967 --> 00:13:04,887
总之 汉弗莱 我还得考虑
Anyway. Humphrey. I have a lot of thinking to do.

257
00:13:04,888 --> 00:13:06,840
我得跟你的前任谈谈
I think I'll talk to your predecessor.

258
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:08,809
阿诺德? 为什么?
Arnold? Why?

259
00:13:08,875 --> 00:13:10,425
我对这种事没经验
I've no experience of this sort of thing.

260
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:12,008
我得请教阿诺德
I have to ask Arnold's advice on

261
00:13:12,009 --> 00:13:15,351
怎么对内阁秘书搞安全调查
setting up a security inquiry on a Cabinet Secretary.

262
00:13:16,593 --> 00:13:19,047
总之 谢谢你 汉弗莱
Anyway, thank you, Humphrey.

263
00:13:20,513 --> 00:13:22,020
没别的事了
That will be all.

264
00:13:22,873 --> 00:13:24,279
好吧...
Yes...

265
00:13:25,699 --> 00:13:27,184
暂时没事了
For the time being.

266
00:13:28,825 --> 00:13:31,038
别跟阿诺德商量 等我先找他
Don't discuss this with Arnold until I've spoken to him.

267
00:13:31,064 --> 00:13:34,721
当然不会 首相 我怎么会是那种人
Of course not, Prime Minister! I wouldn't dream of it.

268
00:13:37,713 --> 00:13:40,181
那你建议我怎么办 阿诺德?
So what do you think I should do, Arnold?

269
00:13:42,513 --> 00:13:42,813
难说
Difficult.

270
00:13:43,481 --> 00:13:46,990
部分取决于你到底是不是间谍
Depends a bit on whether you actually were spying or not.

271
00:13:48,033 --> 00:13:52,106
阿诺德      人总不能有偏见嘛
Arnold!        One must keep an open mind.

272
00:13:52,313 --> 00:13:55,783
可我不可能是 我又没上过剑桥
But I couldn't have been. I wasn't at Cambridge.

273
00:13:58,793 --> 00:14:01,182
我不是他们的人 我有家室
I'm not one of them. I'm a married man.

274
00:14:02,513 --> 00:14:06,267
我是我们的人 当了一辈子公务员了
One of us. I've been in the Civil Service all my life.

275
00:14:06,473 --> 00:14:08,660
约翰霍斯顿也是      对 可他不一样
So had John Halsted.        Yes. But he was different.

276
00:14:08,695 --> 00:14:13,849
怎么?      约翰当年抱有什么信仰 理想
Why?        Well, John used to believe in things. Causes.

277
00:14:13,884 --> 00:14:16,351
我这一生从没有过任何信仰
I've never believed in anything in my life!

278
00:14:18,513 --> 00:14:21,107
他还有想法 独创的想法
He had ideas. Original ideas.

279
00:14:21,273 --> 00:14:23,919
你知道我跟那种事从不沾边
You know I've never done anything like that.

280
00:14:24,254 --> 00:14:28,143
反正 就算你是间谍 我也同意不能捅出去
Anyway. Even if you were spy, I agree it mustn't get out.

281
00:14:28,144 --> 00:14:29,630
真的 阿诺德?
Do you, Arnold?

282
00:14:29,753 --> 00:14:33,769
当然 把信息透给俄国确实很严重
Of course. Giving information to Moscow is serious.

283
00:14:33,804 --> 00:14:35,774
把信息透给任何人都很严重
Giving information to anyone is serious.

284
00:14:35,775 --> 00:14:36,732
比如内阁
The Cabinet.

285
00:14:36,748 --> 00:14:39,494
但这种丑闻 会重创公务员系统威信
But a scandal like this could gravely weaken

286
00:14:39,495 --> 00:14:43,439
所以你绝不能认罪
the authority of the service. You mustn't confess.

287
00:14:43,474 --> 00:14:45,862
可我没罪可认啊
But I haven't done anything to confess to!

288
00:14:45,962 --> 00:14:50,530
就算如此 还有另一种可能
Be that as it may, there is still the other possibility.

289
00:14:50,953 --> 00:14:54,803
为了讨论方便 我们先假设你是无辜的
Let us assume,for the sake of argument,that you are innocent

290
00:14:54,838 --> 00:14:59,122
谢谢 阿诺德      只是假设 绝不含偏见
Oh, thank you, Arnold       Just assuming, without prejudice

291
00:14:59,588 --> 00:15:02,423
那就得考虑失职问题了
Then the question of incompetence arises

292
00:15:02,458 --> 00:15:03,850
可我没失职
But I wasn't incompetent.

293
00:15:03,851 --> 00:15:05,988
是你安排我做调查组秘书
You made me the secretary to the House did the inquiry

294
00:15:06,023 --> 00:15:07,019
你当时明白交待
You made it clear

295
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:09,936
不能查出对他不利的证据
that we were expected to find no evidence against him.

296
00:15:10,313 --> 00:15:11,986
我可不记得
I have no recollections of that.

297
00:15:11,987 --> 00:15:14,881
你心里一清二楚
Oh! You know perfectly well.

298
00:15:14,916 --> 00:15:18,675
你有书面证据吗?      当然没有
You have written evidence of this?       No. Of course not.

299
00:15:18,710 --> 00:15:22,401
那我们接着说你的失职问题
So we return to the question of your incompetence.

300
00:15:22,436 --> 00:15:23,824
你我也许知道
You and I may know

301
00:15:23,825 --> 00:15:26,006
你只是做了份内的事
that you did the job you were required to do,

302
00:15:26,866 --> 00:15:30,232
可这对政客很难解释
but it's hard to explain that to politicians.

303
00:15:30,433 --> 00:15:31,422
非得告诉他们吗?
Do they have to know?

304
00:15:31,423 --> 00:15:35,865
当然 我们尽量避免 危险在于首相
Not if we can help it. The PM is the danger.

305
00:15:36,073 --> 00:15:39,509
他也许会散布出去      那怎么行
He may want to go around to tell people.        He mustn't!

306
00:15:39,673 --> 00:15:41,862
你能制止他吗?      我不知道
Can you stop him?        I don't know.

307
00:15:41,897 --> 00:15:45,343
你必须制止他 要是他告诉内阁呢?
You have to stop him. Suppose he told the Cabinet?

308
00:15:45,344 --> 00:15:48,098
要是内阁把你停职呢?
Suppose they decided to suspend you?

309
00:15:48,273 --> 00:15:52,114
调你去做战争公墓委员会主席呢?
Remove you to the chairmanship of the War Graves Commission

310
00:15:53,513 --> 00:15:56,468
他们无权这样     他们有权 但他们不能
They couldn't!        They could, but they mustn't.

311
00:15:56,503 --> 00:15:58,899
不是因为你 你是可以牺牲的
But not because of you. You are expendable.

312
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:00,845
我不是
I'm not!

313
00:16:01,073 --> 00:16:03,181
一旦树立起原则
Once they accept the principle that

314
00:16:03,182 --> 00:16:06,588
资深公务员可以因失职被罢免
senior civil servants can be removed for incompetence,

315
00:16:06,623 --> 00:16:08,749
这可是导火索
that would be thin end of the wedge.

316
00:16:08,950 --> 00:16:13,417
我们会失去几十名同事 甚至几百名
We could lose dozens of our chaps. Hundreds, perhaps!

317
00:16:13,467 --> 00:16:17,075
几千吧 阿诺德 我该怎么办?
Thousands. Arnold, what am I going to do?

318
00:16:17,110 --> 00:16:20,658
我建议你提升你对首相的重要性
I suggest you make yourself so valuable to the PM

319
00:16:20,659 --> 00:16:21,843
就趁未来几天
over the next few days

320
00:16:21,878 --> 00:16:23,788
让他不能够放你走
that he cannot afford to let you go.

321
00:16:23,823 --> 00:16:29,027
怎么做?      他目前最愁什么?
How?        What is he really dead set on at the moment?

322
00:16:29,062 --> 00:16:30,240
支持率
Popularity.

323
00:16:30,241 --> 00:16:31,198
亲爱的汉弗莱
My dear Humphrey

324
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:34,307
所有政客都愁这个
That is what all politicians are dead set on

325
00:16:34,342 --> 00:16:37,089
可他在近期调查中有所下滑
But he's dropping at the moment in the polls.

326
00:16:37,393 --> 00:16:39,479
那你得把他推上去
Then you must lift him up again.

327
00:16:39,514 --> 00:16:43,879
让他在时下头条新闻中大出风头
Give him a popular role in the biggest current news story.

328
00:16:43,914 --> 00:16:46,041
时下头条新闻是
Well, the biggest current news story is

329
00:16:46,042 --> 00:16:48,336
平原上走失的一条狗
a lost dog on Salisbury Plain.

330
00:16:48,953 --> 00:16:51,547
所以呢?      阿诺德
Well?        Oh, Arnold.

331
00:16:51,713 --> 00:16:53,581
你建议我让首相在
Are you suggesting that I have the Prime Minister

332
00:16:53,582 --> 00:16:55,846
索尔兹伯里平原爬来爬去
crawling all over Salisbury Plain

333
00:16:56,245 --> 00:16:57,871
一手拿探雷器
with a mine detector in one hand and

334
00:16:57,872 --> 00:17:00,202
一手拿袋狗粮?
a packet of Winalot in the other?

335
00:17:02,009 --> 00:17:03,650
大概对英国来说
It would probably do Britain less harm

336
00:17:03,651 --> 00:17:06,000
这是他会做的事之中最无害的
than anything else he'd be likely to be doing.

337
00:17:08,233 --> 00:17:10,317
国防部常任秘书到了
The Permanent Secretary for Defence.

338
00:17:10,318 --> 00:17:12,911
诺曼 谢谢你过来
Norman, good of you to come.

339
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,671
我的国务大臣在内阁干得怎样?
How did my Secretary of State do in Cabinet?

340
00:17:15,833 --> 00:17:18,337
凑合吧 我想内阁开始
Well, so-so. I think Cabinet is starting

341
00:17:18,338 --> 00:17:21,362
怨恨他拒不削减军费的立场了
to resent his refusal to make defence cuts.

342
00:17:21,397 --> 00:17:23,582
可他毫不松口      对
But he didn't back down?        No.

343
00:17:23,753 --> 00:17:25,808
很好 找我什么事?
Excellent. What can I do for you?

344
00:17:25,809 --> 00:17:28,488
有个敏感问题
Well, it's rather a sensitive one.

345
00:17:28,523 --> 00:17:30,639
巡航导弹?      不是
Cruise missiles?        No.

346
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:32,562
星战计划(反弹道导弹系统)?      不是
Star Wars?        No.

347
00:17:33,833 --> 00:17:35,047
那是什么?
What, then?

348
00:17:36,899 --> 00:17:40,415
是索尔兹伯里平原上那条狗
It's this dog on Salisbury Plain.

349
00:17:41,993 --> 00:17:44,783
那个啊 首相抱怨了?
Oh, that! The PM getting his knickers in a twist?

350
00:17:44,784 --> 00:17:47,450
别担心 一切都在掌控之中
Don't worry. It's all under control.

351
00:17:47,485 --> 00:17:50,689
是吗?      没错 本周末保证饿死
Oh, really?        It will starve to death by the weekend.

352
00:17:51,305 --> 00:17:55,937
然后他们会捡回尸体 埋葬在靶场大门口
They'll recover the body and bury it just outside the gates.

353
00:17:55,972 --> 00:17:57,960
卫兵枪口朝下致哀
Guards resting at arms reversed.

354
00:17:57,961 --> 00:18:01,029
司令安慰泪汪汪的小女孩
The C.O. comforting the weeping little girl.

355
00:18:01,070 --> 00:18:02,097
电视台全面报道
Telly will lap it up,

356
00:18:02,098 --> 00:18:05,182
周日报纸刊发动人的图片 毫无问题
We'll get lovely pictures in the Sundays. No problem.

357
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:07,507
救它怎么样?
How about rescuing it?

358
00:18:07,508 --> 00:18:10,956
别傻了 汉弗莱 很危险的
Don't be silly, Humphrey. It's dangerous.

359
00:18:10,991 --> 00:18:13,233
用安全方法救      安全方法?
But to do it safely.       Safely?

360
00:18:13,268 --> 00:18:17,378
你是说一支皇家工兵中队手持探雷器
A squadron of Royal Engineers with mine detectors,

361
00:18:17,379 --> 00:18:20,397
一队兽医手持麻醉枪
the Veterinary Corps with stun darts,

362
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:23,302
一架带一两台绞车的直升机
a helicopter with winching equipment possibly two

363
00:18:23,303 --> 00:18:25,296
一张高达几十万的账单
and a bill up in the hundreds of thousands

364
00:18:25,331 --> 00:18:29,701
就为一条狗 在任何宠物店5块钱就能买到
for a dog you could replace for a five at the local pet shop

365
00:18:29,913 --> 00:18:31,133
但理论上可行?
But it could be done technically ?

366
00:18:31,168 --> 00:18:34,027
理论上什么都可行 有钱的话
Anything can be done technically, if you've got the money.

367
00:18:34,028 --> 00:18:35,353
你能安排吗?
Could you do it?

368
00:18:35,388 --> 00:18:36,648
你疯了吧
You must be mad!

369
00:18:36,649 --> 00:18:40,266
首相正在步步紧逼 要我们削减开支
Here we are under the greatest pressure to cut spending

370
00:18:40,553 --> 00:18:42,647
你建议我们浪费几十万
and you suggest that we waste hundreds of thousands

371
00:18:42,648 --> 00:18:45,629
当着全世界媒体救一条狗
in front of the press on a dog!

372
00:18:45,664 --> 00:18:48,057
这是要我们部门自取灭亡
It would be departmental suicide.

373
00:18:48,092 --> 00:18:52,071
对 可如果有首相授权
Yes, but if the Prime Minister were to authorise it,

374
00:18:52,072 --> 00:18:54,236
如果是他发起的
if it was his initiative,

375
00:18:54,271 --> 00:18:56,469
不就使他更难坚持
wouldn't it make it harder for him to

376
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:59,556
削减国防经费了吗?
insist on defence cuts after that?

377
00:18:59,753 --> 00:19:02,391
汉弗莱 你果真才智过人
Humphrey, you excel yourself.

378
00:19:03,513 --> 00:19:06,270
尤其要瞒着他真实成本
Especially if he didn't find out the true size of

379
00:19:06,271 --> 00:19:09,006
营救结束再汇报
the cost until after the rescue.

380
00:19:09,193 --> 00:19:10,568
你要我怎么做?
What do you want me to do?

381
00:19:11,753 --> 00:19:15,638
做好营救准备 严加保密
Put the rescue operation on standby in strict confidence.

382
00:19:15,673 --> 00:19:18,760
并保证一切功劳归于首相
And promise me the PM will get all the credit.

383
00:19:18,795 --> 00:19:20,817
绝不允许你们国务大臣
No nonsense about your Secretary of State

384
00:19:20,818 --> 00:19:24,601
沾光蹭人气 这是10号的事
trying to muscle in on all the publicity.An NO.10 job

385
00:19:24,636 --> 00:19:26,271
军情五处向你汇报了?
You've been briefed by MI5?

386
00:19:26,272 --> 00:19:29,246
是的 首相 真不幸
Indeed, Prime Minister. Unfortunate.

387
00:19:29,281 --> 00:19:30,669
简直是灾难啊
Disastrous. I said.

388
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:33,319
当然不算灾难 绝不会捅出去的
Not disastrous. Surely It will never come out.

389
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:36,605
事情被大家发现了才算灾难吗?
You mean things are only disastrous if people find out?

390
00:19:36,606 --> 00:19:37,826
当然
Of course.

391
00:19:39,113 --> 00:19:41,270
就算内阁秘书是间谍这种事?
Even if the Cabinet Secretary is a spy?

392
00:19:41,713 --> 00:19:43,479
可我很高兴告诉您 没这回事
I'm happy to say that is not the case.

393
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:44,355
你怎么能肯定?
Why so sure?

394
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:47,986
军情五处刚在霍斯顿文件里找到这个
MI5 have just come across this in the Halsted papers,

395
00:19:47,987 --> 00:19:49,868
他的私人日记
from his private diary.

396
00:19:52,105 --> 00:19:55,363
"又一次会见了那个头号呆瓜阿普比"
"Another session with that prize goof Appleby.

397
00:19:56,774 --> 00:19:58,154
"耍得他团团转"
''Fooled him completely."

398
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,155
"他没提半个棘手的问题"
"He never asked any difficult questions."

399
00:20:00,458 --> 00:20:02,885
"似乎连军情五处报告都没看"
''didn't seem to have read the MI5 report."

400
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,630
"他脑子那么迟钝"
''So much wool in his head"

401
00:20:04,631 --> 00:20:07,432
"糊弄他纯属小菜一碟"
"it's child's play to pull it over his eyes.''

402
00:20:09,633 --> 00:20:13,426
这绝对...      洗清了汉弗莱爵士
That certainly...        Exonerates Sir Humphrey.

403
00:20:13,461 --> 00:20:17,784
阿诺德 我真没法形容我有多开心
Arnold...I can't tell you how happy this makes me.

404
00:20:19,873 --> 00:20:23,707
要不要...      不不 我留着
Shall I...?        No, no. I'll keep this.

405
00:20:25,073 --> 00:20:28,065
就是说没有需要我调查的事了?
I take it there's nothing for me to investigate?

406
00:20:28,273 --> 00:20:30,198
当然 安全方面没有了
Not at all. Not on security grounds.

407
00:20:30,199 --> 00:20:32,303
好 那就不打扰您了
Good. I'll take up no more of your time.

408
00:20:32,338 --> 00:20:35,666
等等 还有失职的问题呢
Hold on. There's still the incompetence.

409
00:20:35,873 --> 00:20:38,829
当然 首相 人非圣贤 孰能无过啊
Well, of course, we all make mistakes.

410
00:20:38,864 --> 00:20:41,825
这过失也太大了 你觉得我该炒他吗?
Not on that scale. Think I should sack him?

411
00:20:41,826 --> 00:20:43,544
恕难同意
I hardly think so.

412
00:20:43,579 --> 00:20:46,302
怎么 公务员永远不该被炒吗?
Why not? Should civil servants never be sacked?

413
00:20:46,303 --> 00:20:48,285
如果他们罪有应得 当然应该
If they deserve it, of course they should

414
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:51,267
在原则上 但实践中不行
In principle, but not in practice.

415
00:20:51,473 --> 00:20:54,733
怎么不行?      那就得发起调查
Why not?        There would have to be an inquiry.

416
00:20:54,768 --> 00:20:58,056
一旦调查起公务员失职问题
All inquiries into the incompetence of civil servants

417
00:20:58,057 --> 00:21:01,431
总会追溯到大臣犯错
somehow seem to be back to mistakes by ministers.

418
00:21:01,466 --> 00:21:04,476
话说回来 还是等我决定吧
On second thoughts, leave it with me.

419
00:21:04,477 --> 00:21:05,999
谢谢 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

420
00:21:13,137 --> 00:21:14,311
汉弗莱爵士到了
Sir Humphrey is outside.

421
00:21:14,473 --> 00:21:17,465
请他进来 伯纳 请他进来
Show him in, Bernard. Show him in!

422
00:21:20,273 --> 00:21:21,902
首相
Prime Minister.

423
00:21:21,937 --> 00:21:25,309
呆瓜 呃...汉弗莱
Goofy. Er, Humphrey.

424
00:21:28,393 --> 00:21:32,511
很高兴告诉你 你的间谍嫌疑洗清了
I'm happy to tell you that you've been cleared of spying.

425
00:21:32,713 --> 00:21:36,220
怎么?      约翰霍斯顿爵士的一份手稿
How?        Something Sir John Halsted wrote.

426
00:21:36,255 --> 00:21:37,918
真令人欣慰
Oh, that's very gratifying.

427
00:21:37,919 --> 00:21:39,446
可不是吗 就知道你会高兴
Isn't it? I knew you will be pleased.

428
00:21:39,481 --> 00:21:40,913
当事人本人可否看看?
May one see the document?

429
00:21:40,914 --> 00:21:42,997
当事人当然可以
One certainly may.

430
00:21:44,673 --> 00:21:47,571
更好的办法 是让别人念给当事人听
Better still, one can have it read to one.

431
00:21:49,428 --> 00:21:50,964
"5月28日
''May 28th.

432
00:21:50,965 --> 00:21:54,792
又一次会见了那个头号呆瓜阿普比
Another session with that prize goof Appleby.

433
00:21:55,379 --> 00:21:56,336
耍得他团团转"
Fooled him completely...''

434
00:21:56,371 --> 00:21:57,574
明白了 谢谢 首相
Yes, I see, while thank you. Prime Minister

435
00:21:57,575 --> 00:22:01,630
不不 接着听 后面洗清得更彻底
No, it goes on. It clears you even more.

436
00:22:02,113 --> 00:22:03,781
"他没问半个棘手的问题
''He never asked any difficult questions.

437
00:22:03,782 --> 00:22:06,387
连军情五处报告..."
didn't seem to have read the MI5 report.''

438
00:22:06,388 --> 00:22:06,878
对 清楚了 多谢
Yes, that's quite clear. Thank you.

439
00:22:06,913 --> 00:22:07,896
"他脑子那么迟钝
''So much wool in his head,

440
00:22:07,897 --> 00:22:10,790
糊弄他纯属小菜一碟"
it's child's play to pull it over his eyes.''

441
00:22:10,791 --> 00:22:12,391
多么精彩啊
Isn't that wonderful?

442
00:22:12,393 --> 00:22:14,162
你一定开心极了
You must be a very happy man.

443
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:19,209
我一直说 霍斯顿不善识人
I always said Halsted was a hopeless judge of character.

444
00:22:19,244 --> 00:22:21,478
你是说这不可信? 他胡扯?
You mean we can't believe this? He was lying?

445
00:22:22,867 --> 00:22:27,011
不不不 不 不 这绝对是真的
Oh, no, no, no. No, no, it's absolutely true.

446
00:22:27,993 --> 00:22:30,233
所谓真 我是说从...
True, that is, in the sense of...

447
00:22:30,678 --> 00:22:33,702
您看 他不够聪明
You see, he wasn't bright enough

448
00:22:33,873 --> 00:22:36,516
不能理解微妙的询问技巧
to understand subtle questioning techniques.

449
00:22:36,517 --> 00:22:38,800
婉转探听法
The non-confrontational approach.

450
00:22:38,835 --> 00:22:43,432
导致他真的平安无事?      不不不
Lulled him into a true sense of security?        No, no, no.

451
00:22:44,513 --> 00:22:46,709
总之 这件事到此结束了?
Anyway, I take it it's all over now?

452
00:22:46,744 --> 00:22:49,141
串通的事结束了
The matter of collusion, yes.

453
00:22:49,142 --> 00:22:52,255
可要是你手下如此失职 你能原谅吗?
But would you condone incompetence of this sort?

454
00:22:52,290 --> 00:22:53,448
都过去这么久了 首相
It was a long time ago. Prime Minister.

455
00:22:53,449 --> 00:22:57,182
我当时压力很大 公务繁忙
I was under great stress. I had many other onerous duties.

456
00:22:57,217 --> 00:22:58,466
你现在也很繁忙啊
You have many other onerous duties now.

457
00:22:58,467 --> 00:23:00,269
对 说实话
Yes. And, in fact...

458
00:23:00,304 --> 00:23:02,736
我一直在思考
..I have been giving some thought to how

459
00:23:02,737 --> 00:23:06,204
您如何才能提高支持率       是吗?
you might increase your popularity rating.      Yes?

460
00:23:06,239 --> 00:23:08,698
强健的政府需要有民望的首相      那么
Strong government needs a popular PM.        So

461
00:23:08,733 --> 00:23:10,763
您应该做些受欢迎的事
What I think you should do something popular.

462
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:11,849
当然 可做什么呢?
Of course. But what?

463
00:23:11,884 --> 00:23:13,448
我正要建议
What I was about to suggest

464
00:23:13,449 --> 00:23:15,446
您能否亲自出面
that you might intervene personally

465
00:23:15,481 --> 00:23:18,649
营救索尔兹伯里平原上可怜的小狗
to save that poor little doggie on Salisbury Plain.

466
00:23:19,045 --> 00:23:21,679
汉弗莱 你说真的?      当然 首相
Humphrey. Are you serious?        Of course. Prime Minister.

467
00:23:23,510 --> 00:23:24,810
这绝对会大受欢迎的
It certainly would be very popular.

468
00:23:24,845 --> 00:23:27,531
成本会很高吗?      当然不会
Would it be very expensive?        Surely not.

469
00:23:27,566 --> 00:23:28,639
我们能担得起吗?
Could we cost it?

470
00:23:29,973 --> 00:23:34,193
依我之见 小本琪时间已经不多了
Well, I gather that time is running out for little Benji.

471
00:23:34,772 --> 00:23:36,712
我们必须今天早晨下决定
We have to make a decision this morning.

472
00:23:37,956 --> 00:23:41,206
人有些时候就得凭良心行事
There are times when you have to act from the heart,

473
00:23:41,207 --> 00:23:43,242
首相也不例外
even as Prime Minister.

474
00:23:44,513 --> 00:23:46,701
你说得对 汉弗莱      可以吗?
You're right, Humphrey!        May I?

475
00:23:46,736 --> 00:23:47,415
拜托了
Please do it.

476
00:23:48,375 --> 00:23:51,870
这不是收买便宜人心的问题 对吧?
It's not a question of buying a little cheap popularity, isn't it?

477
00:23:52,153 --> 00:23:54,223
绝对不是
By no means.

478
00:23:56,113 --> 00:23:57,128
会花很久吗?
Will it take long?

479
00:23:57,129 --> 00:23:59,798
我已经吩咐军队待命三小时
I've got the Army on three-hour standby.

480
00:23:59,799 --> 00:24:01,227
只等您一句话
All I need is your clearance.

481
00:24:01,262 --> 00:24:06,344
太好了      是你吗 诺曼? 开工
Splendid.        Is that you, Norman? Walkies.

482
00:24:08,843 --> 00:24:12,598
终于 本琪 那条走失在
And finally, Benji, the 0ld English sheepdog

483
00:24:12,633 --> 00:24:15,140
索尔兹伯里平原的老英国牧羊犬
lost on the artillery range on Salisbury Plain

484
00:24:15,175 --> 00:24:17,996
已被安全营救 马丁慕卡斯现场报道
has been rescued. Martin Muncaster reports.

485
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:22,575
今天午后 行动从乙区这里展开
The operation began here on B Range early this afternoon.

486
00:24:22,610 --> 00:24:25,505
四队皇家工兵持探雷器
Four detachments of the Royal Engineers with mine detectors

487
00:24:25,506 --> 00:24:26,874
由不同地点出发
set off from different points

488
00:24:26,909 --> 00:24:30,502
向本琪最后出现的地点包抄
to close in on the area where Benji was last sighted.

489
00:24:30,503 --> 00:24:32,834
他们花了一小时找到它
It took them over an hour to locate him.

490
00:24:33,047 --> 00:24:38,425
然后皇家兽医用麻醉枪 让本吉暂时休克
Then the Royal Veterinary Corps fired a stun dart at Benji.

491
00:24:38,633 --> 00:24:40,345
不幸的是 该区域太危险
Unfortunately, the area is too dangerous

492
00:24:40,346 --> 00:24:44,060
引爆所有炸弹又可能伤及狗
to enter without detonating shells which may injure the dog,

493
00:24:44,095 --> 00:24:46,261
因此皇家海军直升机开进现场
so a Royal Navy helicopter was flown in

494
00:24:46,296 --> 00:24:49,242
空中抢险队放下人员救起本琪
and the air rescue team lowered a man to pick up Benji

495
00:24:49,243 --> 00:24:53,037
空运至安全地带 以免穿越危险地面
without crossing the dangerous ground and fly him to safety.

496
00:24:53,072 --> 00:24:57,401
之后 它回到了小主人琳达弗莱彻的怀抱
Later, he was reunited with his young owner, Linda Fletcher

497
00:24:57,436 --> 00:24:58,391
她说她几乎
who said she'd almost

498
00:24:58,392 --> 00:25:00,873
不敢盼望与本琪重聚了
given up hope of ever seeing Benji again.

499
00:25:01,839 --> 00:25:04,056
据悉 是首相的直接干涉
It's understood that it was the direct intervention

500
00:25:04,057 --> 00:25:07,954
促成了此事
from the PM which made the rescue operation possible.

501
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:12,024
亲爱的 你派他们去救狗了      对
Darling, you got them to rescue that dog!        Yes.

502
00:25:12,059 --> 00:25:13,696
你说这是浪费钱的
You said it would be a waste of money.

503
00:25:13,697 --> 00:25:15,573
我知道 但我考虑了你的话
I know, and I thought what you said.

504
00:25:15,574 --> 00:25:17,095
政府应该关心嘛
government is caring.

505
00:25:17,130 --> 00:25:21,257
关心选票?      别这么刻薄 安妮
Caring about votes?        That's not very kind, Annie.

506
00:25:21,542 --> 00:25:22,809
我想到那个小女孩
I thought about that little girl

507
00:25:22,810 --> 00:25:27,079
还有本琪对她的意义 个人的确有分量
and what Benji must mean to her. Individuals do count,

508
00:25:27,214 --> 00:25:29,872
即使在一个预算和收支平衡表的世界里
even in a world of budgets and balance sheets.

509
00:25:30,153 --> 00:25:32,645
有些人可能会批评我滥用军队
Some people might criticise me make using the army that way

510
00:25:32,713 --> 00:25:34,656
可有时候 做正确的事
but sometimes doing the right thing

511
00:25:34,657 --> 00:25:37,243
就得牺牲些民望
means risking unpopularity.

512
00:25:37,353 --> 00:25:41,755
我可不会批评你 亲爱的 我觉得你太棒了
Well,I won't criticise you,darling.I think you're wonderful.

513
00:25:44,913 --> 00:25:45,822
看到了吗 汉弗莱?
See this, Humphrey?

514
00:25:45,854 --> 00:25:49,007
"英国今天明白了 还有一颗真正的人心
''Britain learned today that a real human heart

515
00:25:49,008 --> 00:25:51,432
在唐宁街10号跳动"
beats inside Number 10 Downing Street.''

516
00:25:51,461 --> 00:25:54,839
实际上 有74颗人心在这里跳呢
Actually, 74 human hearts beat inside NO.10 Downing Street

517
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:56,217
谢谢 伯纳
Thank you, Bernard.

518
00:25:56,865 --> 00:26:00,535
瞧 我说得对 我凭直觉就知道人们的需求
See? I was right. I have an instinct for what people want.

519
00:26:01,078 --> 00:26:03,241
恕我直言 首相...
If I may say so, Prime Minister...

520
00:26:03,242 --> 00:26:06,375
当然 是你的主意 对吗?
Of course! It was your idea, wasn't it?

521
00:26:06,393 --> 00:26:09,480
干得好 我能怎么报答你呢?
Well done. What can I do for you?

522
00:26:09,515 --> 00:26:11,835
霍斯顿调查?
The Halsted inquiry?

523
00:26:11,836 --> 00:26:14,323
不用再提了 我彻底忘了
Say no more about it. Completely forgotten.

524
00:26:14,358 --> 00:26:17,760
谢谢 首相 可以讨论内阁议程了吗?
Oh, thank you.PM. Now may we discuss the Cabinet agenda?

525
00:26:17,761 --> 00:26:19,464
有一两件事
One or two points.

526
00:26:19,499 --> 00:26:21,037
第3项...
Item 3...

527
00:26:21,038 --> 00:26:24,061
琳达说"我投哈克先生一票"
Linda says, ''My vote goes to Mr Hacker!''

528
00:26:26,513 --> 00:26:29,086
您说什么?      对不起 汉弗莱 什么?
I beg your pardon?        I'm sorry, Humphrey. Yes?

529
00:26:32,113 --> 00:26:34,707
"BBC和ITV接到潮水般的电话"
''BBC and ITV report a flood of phone calls,

530
00:26:34,873 --> 00:26:38,582
"人们交口称赞首相营救本琪的决定"
''all approving the PM's decision to rescue Benji.''

531
00:26:38,793 --> 00:26:41,990
我能否建议我们推迟第3项 首相?
May I suggest that we postpone Item 3, Prime Minister?

532
00:26:42,153 --> 00:26:45,154
"反对党领袖拒不出面评论"
'The Leader of the Opposition was not available for comment'

533
00:26:45,155 --> 00:26:46,429
谅他也不敢
I bet he wasn't!

534
00:26:46,464 --> 00:26:49,842
要么支持我 要么让宠物狗饿死
Support me or let pet dogs starve to death!

535
00:26:50,517 --> 00:26:51,976
我真把他难住了 对吧?
I really had him there, didn't I?

536
00:26:52,011 --> 00:26:54,590
抱歉 汉弗莱      第3项 首相
Sorry, Humphrey.        Item 3. Prime Minister.

537
00:26:54,625 --> 00:26:59,150
对 第3项是什么? 削减军费? 怎么啦?
Item 3. Yes, what's Item 3? Defence cuts? What about them?

538
00:26:59,185 --> 00:27:02,789
我建议 先提交内阁委员会讨论
I'm going to suggest we'd refer them to Cabinet Committee.

539
00:27:02,993 --> 00:27:05,077
不行 我要本周四出决定
No, I want a decision on Thursday,

540
00:27:05,078 --> 00:27:06,944
不要明年三月一份60页的报告
not a 60-page submission next Easter.

541
00:27:06,979 --> 00:27:12,087
啊 可我刚刚收到了预估的
Ah, because I've just had the provisional costings

542
00:27:12,122 --> 00:27:14,471
救狗行动成本
for the dog rescue operation.

543
00:27:18,513 --> 00:27:21,311
31万英镑?
310,000?

544
00:27:21,473 --> 00:27:22,800
不可能
That's impossible!

545
00:27:22,801 --> 00:27:25,807
这是国防部根据实际成本计算的
Those are MOD figures on a true-cost basis.

546
00:27:25,928 --> 00:27:27,954
太荒唐了 汉弗莱 得想点办法
This is absurd. We must do something.

547
00:27:27,955 --> 00:27:29,187
把狗放回去?
Put the dog back?

548
00:27:31,201 --> 00:27:35,018
岂有此理 反正我不延迟第3项
That's ridiculous. Anyhow I'm not postponing Item 3.

549
00:27:35,019 --> 00:27:36,964
由您决定 首相
Well, it's your decision, Prime Minister.

550
00:27:36,999 --> 00:27:40,624
真是有魄力的决定 容我这么说
And a very courageous one, if I may say so.

551
00:27:41,289 --> 00:27:43,791
有魄力? 为什么?
Courageous? Why?

552
00:27:43,826 --> 00:27:46,332
如果真的削减了军费
Well, if the defence cuts are made,

553
00:27:46,333 --> 00:27:49,201
救狗的成本肯定会被漏给媒体
the cost of rescuing a dog is bound to be leaked to the press

554
00:27:49,236 --> 00:27:50,052
不是吧
Oh, no.

555
00:27:50,053 --> 00:27:54,720
除非您完全信任国防部的保密工作
Unless you have faith in MOD confidentiality in loyalty.

556
00:27:54,793 --> 00:27:57,167
别傻了 他们漏得跟筛子一样
Don't be absurd! Of course, they leak like sieves.

557
00:27:57,951 --> 00:27:58,956
结果可想而知
I can see it now.

558
00:27:58,957 --> 00:28:03,675
"首相救狗 英国空军买单"
"PM saves dog at expense of Britain's air defences"

559
00:28:03,710 --> 00:28:06,406
多劲爆的故事      一个落水狗的故事
It would be quite a story.        A shaggy dog story.

560
00:28:08,753 --> 00:28:11,227
可消息不会泄露 除非...
But it would only come out if...

561
00:28:11,567 --> 00:28:14,922
我不吃勒索这一套      当然不
I'm not going to be blackmailed.        Of course not.

562
00:28:20,713 --> 00:28:24,564
话说回来 军费也不能削减过分
On the other hand, one can cut defence too far.

563
00:28:24,599 --> 00:28:26,995
当然
Absolutely.

564
00:28:27,790 --> 00:28:29,925
领土防卫 政府第一要务
Defence of the realm. First duty of government.

565
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,153
第一要务
First duty.

566
00:28:31,154 --> 00:28:34,770
总有紧急情况 朝鲜 马岛
There are emergencies - Korea, the Falklands.

567
00:28:34,833 --> 00:28:37,769
本琪      本琪 对
Benji.        Benji! Yes.

568
00:28:39,248 --> 00:28:41,058
我想我是太急进了点
I think I may have been a little hasty.

569
00:28:41,059 --> 00:28:44,422
对 第3项还需要多加考虑
Yes,I think Item 3 probably needs a bit more thought.

570
00:28:44,457 --> 00:28:46,233
再明智不过了
I'm sure that's wise.

571
00:28:46,234 --> 00:28:47,249
不能着急
And there is no hurry.

572
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,165
把削减军费的事提交委员会 好吗?
Refer defence cuts to committee, would you?

573
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,214
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

574
00:28:54,361 --> 00:29:04,472
<font color="#4096d1">破烂熊字幕组-==www.RagBear.com==-
